A combo box needs a combo box cell, and the private key Qt reads off it.

NSComboBox never overrode +cellClass, so every combo box carried the NSTextFieldCell it inherited
from NSTextField: the drop-down state lived nowhere, and NSComboBoxCell, fully present in this
tree, was never used by the control it exists for.

What made it fatal rather than cosmetic: Qt macstyle highlights the arrow of an editable combo via

    [[[combo cell] valueForKey: @"_buttonCell"] setHighlighted: pressed]

during EVERY QComboBox paint, and _buttonCell is a real NSComboBoxCell ivar on macOS. Here the
cell was an NSTextFieldCell, KVC fell through to valueForUndefinedKey:, and the uncaught exception
killed CMake.app inside its first makeKeyAndOrderFront. +cellClass now answers NSComboBoxCell, and
NSComboBoxCell answers _buttonCell with a lazily created NSButtonCell held as an associated
object, a METHOD rather than an ivar so the layout every archived cell depends on stays put. The
highlight lands on a valid cell; nothing reads it back yet.

With this, CMake.app RENDERS AND RESIZES for the first time: titled window, traffic lights, menu
bar, retitles on resize, zero faults and zero exceptions. The content pane is still empty, which
is the next defect. Task #227.

--- a/AppKit/NSComboBox.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSComboBox.m
@@ -34,6 +34,14 @@
 
 @implementation NSComboBox
 
+/* NSTextField's cellClass was inherited, so every combo box carried a plain NSTextFieldCell: the
+ * drop-down state lived nowhere, and Qt asking the cell for its _buttonCell (a real macOS ivar)
+ * raised valueForUndefinedKey and killed CMake.app in its first paint. Task #227. */
++ (Class) cellClass {
+    return [NSComboBoxCell class];
+}
+
+
 - dataSource {
     return [[self cell] dataSource];
 }
--- a/AppKit/NSComboBoxCell.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSComboBoxCell.m
@@ -28,6 +28,28 @@
 
 @implementation NSComboBoxCell
 
+/*
+ * THE PRIVATE KEY QT READS. Qt macstyle highlights the drop-down arrow of an editable combo with
+ *
+ *     [[[combo cell] valueForKey: @"_buttonCell"] setHighlighted: pressed]
+ *
+ * and on macOS NSComboBoxCell carries that ivar. This cell models its arrow as two BOOLs, so KVC
+ * fell through to valueForUndefinedKey: and the exception killed CMake.app during its FIRST paint.
+ * A METHOD satisfies the same key without touching the ivar layout every archived cell depends on;
+ * the returned cell exists so the highlight has somewhere valid to land, and nothing reads it back
+ * yet. Task #227.
+ */
+- (NSButtonCell *) _buttonCell {
+    static const void *key = &key;
+    NSButtonCell *cell = objc_getAssociatedObject(self, key);
+    if (cell == nil) {
+        cell = [[[NSButtonCell alloc] initImageCell: nil] autorelease];
+        objc_setAssociatedObject(self, key, cell, OBJC_ASSOCIATION_RETAIN_NONATOMIC);
+    }
+    return cell;
+}
+
+
 - (void) encodeWithCoder: (NSCoder *) coder {
     NSUnimplementedMethod();
 }
